The original ask has not yet been fully met. You still need to rename the “left–association” method and its call site.

1. In buttonClicked (line 321), change  
   ```java
   else if (buttonCode == 13) newEdge = addAssocClassLeft(mgm, cls, newNode);
   ```  
   to  
   ```java
   else if (buttonCode == 13) newEdge = createEdgeLeft(mgm, cls, newNode);
   ```

2. Rename the helper method at lines 347–350:  
   ```java
   public Object addAssocClassLeft(MutableGraphModel mgm, MClass cls,
                                   MClass newCls) {
       return mgm.connect(newCls, cls, MAssociation.class);
   }
   ```  
   →  
   ```java
   public Object createEdgeLeft(MutableGraphModel mgm, MClass cls,
                                MClass newCls) {
       return mgm.connect(newCls, cls, MAssociation.class);
   }
   ```

After these two renames are applied, all “addAssocClass…” identifiers will consistently be “createEdgeRight” or “createEdgeLeft,” and the task will be complete.  

