40: /**
41:  * The checkbox to be used to show boolean attributes in the GUI's. Mostly used
42:  * on proppanels. The other new GUI elements (like UMLLinkedList) divide the 
43:  * responsibility of showing an attribute and maintaining the state of the 
44:  * attribute between a GUI element and a model. This is not the case for the 
45:  * UMLCheckBox2. Reason for this is that the model is just to simple to allow
46:  * extra classes for the model. 
47:  * 
48:  * @since Oct 12, 2002
49:  * @author jaap.branderhorst@xs4all.nl
50:  */
51: public abstract class UMLCheckBox2
52:     extends JCheckBox
